    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all its tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nTelephone handling now stores and returns numbers in **E.164 form**, replacing the old 10-digit behaviour.\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/E164Telephone.java`\n- `normalize(raw)`: strips every non-digit (spaces, dashes, brackets); if the input starts with `+`, keeps the country code; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits; requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, else throws `InvalidTelephoneException` (\u2192 400).\n- `normalizeOrNull(raw)`: best-effort variant for comparing existing owners.\n\nI put this in a plain utility class rather than adding a method to the function class, because OfficeFloor requires **exactly one public method per wired function** \u2014 my first attempt added `toE164` to `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` and broke startup with `Require configuring method for normalizeTelephone ... multiple public methods`.\n\n**Updated files**\n- `NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java` \u2014 now delegates to `E164Telephone.normalize(...)`, mutating the body in place so the stored `Owner` and the response carry the E.164 string.\n- `RejectDuplicateTelephone.java` \u2014 duplicate detection now compares E.164 values (normalizing each existing owner's telephone) instead of stripped 10-digit strings.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 replaced the `@Digits`/`@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")` constraints (which JPA enforces on persist) with `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` so the E.164 value validates; removed the now-unused `@Digits` import.\n- Refreshed the stale Javadoc on `InvalidTelephoneException` / `InvalidTelephoneHandler`.\n\n**Verified against the spec's tests**: `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`; `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`; `12` \u2192 400. Full `./mvnw -o test` is **BUILD SUCCESS** (3/3).\n\nOne note: the POST create pipeline reads the raw body without `@Valid`, so I left `openapi.yml`'s `telephone` pattern (`^[0-9]*$`) untouched \u2014 it isn't enforced on this path and no test exercises it. If you later add `@Valid`-based validation to the create/update path, that pattern would also need relaxing to permit the leading `+`.",
